Subject: [PATCH 1/3] PUBLISH-FIX-103: two drills that only passed on a laptop

lib/config.js dataDir() is COBRA_DATA_DIR + SERPENT_DATA_GENERATION.
Both drills set COBRA_DATA_DIR to their own temp root and left the
generation to the ambient shell - and the Replit shell exports
SERPENT_DATA_GENERATION=gen1. So the write went to <tmp>/gen1 and the
read looked in <tmp>: green on a laptop, red on the deployment host.

  test/universe.test.js      not ok 7 - a failed venue refresh withdraws
                             new admission truth ...
  test/tape-hot-lane.test.js not ok 3 - the current-universe record
                             becomes a superset of the carried hot pairs

Both now pin the generation off and restore it, so a drill owns its own
data root whatever the shell says. Verified green BOTH ways:
SERPENT_DATA_GENERATION=gen1 -> 9/9 and 4/4; unset -> 9/9 and 4/4.

No source change. A "passes here, fails there" drill is how a real bug
hides, and I had been unsetting the variable by hand to get a green
line, which is the same thing as not running it.

