From 41f5824572371b09e76dccd9c8dfcdc406a1afae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] PUBLISH-FIX-104: a THIRD six, in a third file, clamping
 the policy

FIX-99 widened the tape's hot lane 6 -> 20 on measured headroom.
FIX-100 widened policy.universe.preparationSlots and maxCandidates
6 -> 20 and bound a NEW $500 account to do it, because a policy binding
is immutable per account. Deployment dc6e5638 logged

  HOT LANE: POL joins the deep tape now (... hot slots 20/20)

and the very next funnel line read

  JUDGE FUNNEL: 6 candidates; books 61413 ...

judge/readiness.js carried `export const PREP_SLOTS_MAX = 6`, applied
as Math.min(PREP_SLOTS_MAX, remainingSlots). It is a CEILING that had
been set to exactly the number the policy used to say - so the policy
could be widened, the account rebound, and twenty order books carried,
and the Judge would still prepare six, silently, for ever.

The policy is the authority: it is digest-bound to the account and
cannot change without a new one. This constant only refuses an absurd
value, so it is 64 now, not a second opinion about the number. Nothing
else in selectPreparation moved - ranking, warm-up protection, the
FIX-12 fair rotation, the TTL, held-asset exclusion and the loss
reasons are byte-for-byte, and a policy asking for six still gets six.

test/publish-fix-104-no-third-six.test.js walks the WHOLE chain -
shipped config -> composition's Math.min(preparationSlots,
maxCandidates) -> the slots actually selected - and asserts the
narrowest point of the last stage is 20, so a fourth six in a fourth
file cannot hide either.

Frozen: judge 6e7022571afd -> 9122a83068c6, all d393d661b0b6 ->
39a03bf6645e; execution and watch/watch.js unchanged. Recorded as
docs/JUDGE-PAPER-AUDIT.md 4.40.

