From cd6a974e0ce38f94cd55ae81c635cd143f59f2f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] PUBLISH-FIX-105: the instrument that answers "why" runs
 one minute in ten

One sampled top-frames minute in THIRTY meant that when the loop was
saturated - 87% tonight at twenty order books - the only line that says
what the main thread was doing arrived once every half hour, and the
first one after a boot described the boot, not the running app.

At one in ten the instrument costs about 0.4% of the thread on average
and the app can always answer the question that found tonight's real
hog:

  CPU PROFILE 60s: top: fsync 40% 4793ms . update 16% . (gc) 6%
                   . readFileUtf8 4% . writeBuffer 4% . open 2%

The every-minute CPU LOAD line (event-loop utilization, no profiler at
all) is unchanged. Diagnostic only; authority NONE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RoFoPS22WFW1oUnbWzPayd
